## WHAT IS REDBLUE?

Redblue is a programming language designed to be as readable as plain English.

**Example Code:**
```redblue
say "Hello, World!"

set name to "World"
if name is "World"
    say "Hello, {name}!"
end

to add(a, b)
=== SPEC 565-575
end
```

### Return Values

```redblue
to add(a, b)
    give back a + b
end

to max(a, b)
=== SPEC 973-982

`might fail <call>` discards a failure of that call and produces `nothing`, so
the program carries on where it would otherwise have stopped:

```redblue
set config to might fail files.read("config.rb")
if config is nothing
    say "using defaults"
end
```
=== SPEC 603-612
```

### First-Class Functions

```redblue
set double to to (x) give back x * 2

set numbers to [1, 2, 3]
set doubled to numbers.map(double)
```
